Pass the Impeller context to LayerTree::Flatten (backport).

Backport of flutter/flutter#191017 (commit bb8568060, "Makes sure impeller
context's are plumbed through to LayerTree::Flatten", fixes
flutter/flutter#190774), which isn't in 3.44.

With Impeller, snapshotting a layer tree that holds an external texture
(Scene.toImageSync, which page transitions use, while a video is on
screen) flattened it without the Impeller context, so the embedder's GL
texture took the Skia path and called flushAndSubmit on a null
GrDirectContext: a segfault on the raster thread. Seen in Kudos when
leaving the welcome screen with its video playing.

The upstream change applied as is, except two files that differ in 3.44
and were ported by hand: lib/ui/snapshot_delegate.h (the same three
additions) and lib/ui/painting/picture.cc (3.44 has no is_impeller_enabled
there, so Impeller is told by the delegate having an AiksContext). Its unit
tests are included but aren't part of the release build.

